From: Stained Glass OS <dev@stained-glass.example>
Subject: shell32: image thumbnails

An image thumbnail provider of our own (IThumbnailProvider with
IInitializeWithStream/IInitializeWithFile over WIC: PNG, JPEG, BMP, GIF, TIFF,
icons), registered for those types as Windows registers its own
(ShellEx\{e357fccd-...}); never enlarged, shrunk by averaging, JPEG EXIF
orientation applied. A file type's handler is found where Windows looks (the
extension, SystemFileAssociations, the ProgID); an older IExtractImage
handler is used when there is no IThumbnailProvider (IExtractImage,
IExtractImage2 and IInitializeWithItem are added to shobjidl.idl).
IShellItemImageFactory::GetImage, a stub, now returns the thumbnail, else the
icon at the size asked for, with its alpha.

Gate: test/explorer2-gate.sh (a PNG's and a JPEG's pixels in the view).
